{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Reclaim duplicate storage for eligible identical immutable payload files in release-cache.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The two root:root mode-0644 payload copies were initially separate, were safely replaced with one shared inode, and retained link count 2. Reported disk usage shows one 4096-byte allocation reclaimed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-63b2a7761e424b32","cmd-bb4daae755d44fab","cmd-40ca74c3d68f4054"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve every pathname, byte, and mode; keep different-permission files independent and mutable files independently writable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All five original paths remain with baseline hashes and modes. private.dat remains mode 0600 on an independent inode, different.dat retains its distinct content, and mutable/active.dat remains mode 0644, writable, link-count 1, and independent from the payload inode. These properties also survived restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-40ca74c3d68f4054","cmd-fc6a26e1e7d342e2"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Ensure a later cache pass makes no further changes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Repeat checks before and after restart both found the eligible payload paths already linked and reported changed=0.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0b73b75230bc4fe0","cmd-8d8dd12d6d714631"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use legacy-platform-compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 7.9 and kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64 are identical before and after execution. The complete timeline shows only existing platform utilities being used and no package installation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1ce708363aed4314","cmd-97e3cca8d5eb4eeb","cmd-fc6a26e1e7d342e2","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"No unnecessary state-changing mutation was observed: the hardlink replacement directly fulfilled the task, and the restart served the mandatory provider protocol. The restart command launched successfully enough to reboot but then failed while printing its acknowledgement because NODE_NAME was unset. It also left an empty /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log file, which remained after execution and is minor unwanted residue. Restart-generated PID and systemd-private-directory changes are expected; no failed services or new listening endpoints were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bb4daae755d44fab","cmd-c5a1047a1009400c","cmd-93a7bf6f76234f5b","cmd-e281433694474ed9","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are directly demonstrated. The eligible payload pair now shares storage, all content and required metadata are preserved, protected and mutable files remain independent, repeat passes are idempotent, and the original RHEL release and kernel remain installed. Restart evidence shows a healthy pre-state, bounded loss of connectivity, a changed boot identity, and full recovered system and data state; fixed lifecycle boot observations corroborate the transition.","limitations":["The restart scheduling command produced no explicit restart-acknowledgement output because it failed on an unset NODE_NAME after launching the delayed shutdown. The subsequent outage, changed boot ID, reboot history, and recovered state strongly demonstrate that the restart occurred, but the provider protocol's acknowledgement element is formally incomplete.","Package-health collection timed out both before and after execution, so package-manager consistency was not independently verified; the command timeline contains no package mutation."]}
